{"version":1,"slug":"photosynthesis","topic":"How does photosynthesis work?","level":"beginner","title":"How Photosynthesis Works","summary":"By the end, you will understand how plants turn sunlight, water, and air into their own food and the oxygen we breathe.","scopeNote":null,"scenes":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","title":"How does photosynthesis work?","segments":[{"id":"intro-0","narration":"Have you ever wondered how a giant oak tree builds itself out of thin air, water, and sunlight?","sig":"w3lejl2A8Gmbk_Ho46DoHVURsERHo-5I","actions":[{"id":"hero","kind":"icon","cue":"Have you ever","text":"Sunlight into food","items":null,"icon":"leaf","at":{"col":0,"row":1,"w":4,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"intro-1","narration":"Here's our plan. First, Plants Make Their Own Food. Then, Inside the Leaf Factory. And finally, Why It Matters to Us.","sig":"qTOI1jS9L5f8BUFsWq17ARiy46MgPrTQ","actions":[{"id":"agenda","kind":"list","cue":"Here's our plan","text":null,"items":["Plants Make Their Own Food","Inside the Leaf Factory","Why It Matters to Us"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":5,"row":1,"w":7,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c1","kind":"chapter","title":"Plants Make Their Own Food","segments":[{"id":"c1-0","narration":"You might think plants eat soil through their roots to grow. Actually, that is a common myth!","sig":"DKrm3gftaKmzPOg_x-JuWmnbmbELswhF","actions":[{"id":"soil_myth","kind":"note","cue":"plants eat soil","text":"Myth: Plants eat soil","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":0,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"red","expr":null},{"id":"x_myth","kind":"cross_out","cue":"a common myth","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"soil_myth","color":"red","expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-1","narration":"Instead, plants are like tiny chefs that build their own sugar right inside their leaves.","sig":"jdlqIHe9ApwqrrNsSXp8JNafXDCwTa5Z","actions":[{"id":"sugar","kind":"box","cue":"build their own sugar","text":"Builds own sugar","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":9,"row":2,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"chk_sugar","kind":"check","cue":"build their own sugar","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"sugar","color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"leaf","kind":"icon","cue":"inside their leaves","text":"Leaf Kitchen","items":null,"icon":"leaf","at":{"col":5,"row":2,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"a_leaf_sugar","kind":"arrow","cue":"inside their leaves","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"leaf","to":"sugar","target":null,"color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-2","narration":"To cook up that sugar, a leaf pulls in three simple ingredients: sunlight from above, water from the roots, and carbon dioxide from the air.","sig":"U2zXIOypgsj8ktz4TiPrbyas2T0XIL3V","actions":[{"id":"sun","kind":"icon","cue":"sunlight from above","text":"Sunlight","items":null,"icon":"sun","at":{"col":5,"row":0,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"a_sun","kind":"arrow","cue":"sunlight from above","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"sun","to":"leaf","target":null,"color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"water","kind":"icon","cue":"water from the roots","text":"Water","items":null,"icon":"droplet","at":{"col":1,"row":3,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"a_water","kind":"arrow","cue":"water from the roots","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"water","to":"leaf","target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-3","narration":"The water travels up to the leaf, and carbon dioxide drifts in through tiny holes, giving the plant everything it needs.","sig":"ygDBKDmZGWwWZYj5mv2jDocafxGDbJC0","actions":[{"id":"t_water","kind":"trace","cue":"water travels up","text":null,"items":null,"icon":"droplet","at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"a_water","color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"co2","kind":"box","cue":"carbon dioxide drifts in","text":"Carbon Dioxide","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":8,"row":0,"w":3,"h":1},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"a_co2","kind":"arrow","cue":"carbon dioxide drifts in","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"co2","to":"leaf","target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"p_leaf","kind":"pulse","cue":"everything it needs","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"leaf","color":"green","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c2","kind":"chapter","title":"Inside the Leaf Factory","segments":[{"id":"c2-0","narration":"Now that you know plants make their own food, let us peek inside the leaf factory. A green pigment called chlorophyll acts like tiny solar panels, capturing energy from sunlight.","sig":"6DJTD9WT7Pes3PQ-o7ztNO8dAnTGiDYu","actions":[{"id":"leaf_factory","kind":"box","cue":"inside the leaf factory","text":"Chlorophyll","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":2,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"sun","kind":"icon","cue":"capturing energy from sunlight","text":"Sunlight","items":null,"icon":"sun","at":{"col":0,"row":0,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"a_sun","kind":"arrow","cue":"from sunlight","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"sun","to":"leaf_factory","target":null,"color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"t_sun","kind":"trace","cue":"from sunlight","text":null,"items":null,"icon":"zap","at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"a_sun","color":"orange","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-1","narration":"Chlorophyll uses that solar energy to split water molecules apart. Think of it like snapping Lego bricks so you can build something new.","sig":"Ifo8EO62981Wv5J-2OHGyE8rrjI0aXov","actions":[{"id":"water","kind":"icon","cue":"split water molecules","text":"Water","items":null,"icon":"droplet","at":{"col":0,"row":3,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"a_water","kind":"arrow","cue":"split water molecules","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"water","to":"leaf_factory","target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"t_water","kind":"trace","cue":"snapping Lego bricks","text":null,"items":null,"icon":"droplet","at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"a_water","color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-2","narration":"Next, the leaf combines those pieces with carbon dioxide from the air.","sig":"GvgzBN0W9-9Y47d4yQ65FcVVoqHBnwZ1","actions":[{"id":"co2","kind":"box","cue":"carbon dioxide","text":"Carbon Dioxide","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":0,"w":3,"h":1},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"ink","expr":null},{"id":"a_co2","kind":"arrow","cue":"from the air","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"co2","to":"leaf_factory","target":null,"color":"ink","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-3","narration":"That reaction builds energy-rich sugar for the plant and releases fresh oxygen.","sig":"Ta_dDOyNYAO9zNfLaiLOE64_idlm1pAO","actions":[{"id":"sugar","kind":"box","cue":"energy-rich sugar","text":"Sugar (Food)","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":9,"row":0,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"a_sugar","kind":"arrow","cue":"for the plant","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"leaf_factory","to":"sugar","target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"oxygen","kind":"box","cue":"releases fresh oxygen","text":"Oxygen","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":9,"row":3,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"a_oxygen","kind":"arrow","cue":"fresh oxygen","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"leaf_factory","to":"oxygen","target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c3","kind":"chapter","title":"Why It Matters to Us","segments":[{"id":"c3-0","narration":"Now that we know how the leaf factory makes sugar and oxygen, let's see why that matters to you and me. Plants release oxygen into the air, and every animal, including you, breathes it in.","sig":"iKrDbULAc6qiC3U0rYBu53h62kw3mkph","actions":[{"id":"life_cycle","kind":"cycle","cue":"why that matters","text":null,"items":["Tree","Oxygen","Animal","Carbon dioxide"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":0,"w":7,"h":6},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"p_o2","kind":"pulse","cue":"release oxygen","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"life_cycle[1]","color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-1","narration":"When we breathe out, we send carbon dioxide back to the trees, keeping a giant life cycle spinning.","sig":"FI2IN8xtHh-faMYJ9PBH13RUfl7sVm2c","actions":[{"id":"tr_cycle","kind":"trace","cue":"life cycle spinning","text":null,"items":null,"icon":"wind","at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"life_cycle","color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-2","narration":"Even better, the sugar plants make powers entire food chains, from tiny bugs to giant whales. Without photosynthesis, life on Earth simply could not exist.","sig":"RB4gvflO94_PetjaY50Gwm4ZzU4bsWH9","actions":[{"id":"support_note","kind":"note","cue":"powers entire food chains","text":"Plants support all life","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":8,"row":1,"w":4,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"hl_support","kind":"highlight","cue":"life on Earth","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"support_note","color":"orange","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"recap","kind":"recap","title":"Recap","segments":[{"id":"recap-0","narration":"To recap: plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to build sugar. Inside leaves, chlorophyll powers this reaction and releases oxygen. That gives us food and air!","sig":"OEJzweWB14JVWqaOnEE-ytx8Jci0G7Ov","actions":[{"id":"recap_list","kind":"list","cue":"To recap: plants use","text":null,"items":["Plants make sugar from three ingredients","Chlorophyll uses light, releases oxygen","Powers food chains and our air"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":1,"row":1,"w":6,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"ink","expr":null},{"id":"recap_leaf","kind":"icon","cue":"food and air","text":"Photosynthesis","items":null,"icon":"leaf","at":{"col":8,"row":2,"w":3,"h":3},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"recap-1","narration":"Got any questions about photosynthesis? Just ask!","sig":"w3uxB5AL8g1sea1zJphPMvVsca57sVzp","actions":[{"id":"recap_pulse","kind":"pulse","cue":"Got any questions","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"recap_leaf","color":"green","expr":null}]}]}],"quiz":[{"question":"Where do plants get the carbon dioxide they need to make sugar?","options":["From the soil","From sunlight","From the air","From their roots"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Carbon dioxide drifts into the leaf through tiny holes from the surrounding air.","chapter":1},{"question":"What is the main job of chlorophyll inside a leaf?","options":["Capture energy from sunlight","Pull water from the roots","Breathe in oxygen","Store sugar in the stem"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Chlorophyll acts like tiny solar panels that capture sunlight to power the leaf factory.","chapter":2},{"question":"How do animals and plants help each other in the air cycle?","options":["Animals give plants sugar","Plants breathe in oxygen","Animals make sunlight","Plants give oxygen, animals give carbon dioxide"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Plants release oxygen that animals breathe in, and animals breathe out carbon dioxide that plants use.","chapter":3}],"suggestions":["How do plants drink water?","What is cellular respiration?","How do food chains work?"],"models":{"lesson":"google/gemini-4-hydrogen","voice":"google/gemini-3.8-flash-tts"},"createdAt":"2026-11-17T12:45:12.644Z","audioBase":"/samples/photosynthesis"}